              "size_bytes": 242909
            },
            "native_start": 60,
            "native_end": 172,
            "text": "the \"Colorado Municipal Election Code of 1965\", article 10 of title 31, C.R.S., with respect to \nany election. \n",
            "text_sha256": "0eb5039f1f2c9f7cc5451276194d0d3e3f045c7ecd722f7f9f276809ad9be223",
            "visible_location": "First two body lines",
            "source_review_qualification": "Continuation of(1), not a new unlabeled paragraph.",
            "byte_basis": "half_open_utf8_offsets_in_unchanged_native_page"
          }
        ],
        "text": "(1)    This code applies to all general, primary, congressional vacancy, school district, special \ndistrict, ballot issue, and other authorized elections unless otherwise provided by this code. This \ncode applies to any municipal election conducted as part of a coordinated election except to the \nextent that this code conflicts with a specific charter provision. Any municipality may provide by \nordinance or resolution that it will utilize the requirements and procedures of this code in lieu of \nthe \"Colorado Municipal Election Code of 1965\", article 10 of title 31, C.R.S., with respect to \nany election. \n",
        "text_sha256": "215c21fdad9f92f204050d2366729a5092ca44e41c0c1ff2d23fff6aabbaa621",
        "continuation_note": "Physical4 bottom continues on5 before(2).",
        "byte_basis": "ordered_native_fragments_concatenated_without_insertions"
      },
      {
        "label": "(2)",
        "fragments": [
          {
            "region_id": "S102-B2",
            "section_id": "CRS-1-1-102",
            "role": "statutory_paragraph",
            "physical_page": 5,
            "printed_page": "-5-",
            "native": {
              "path": "native/page-0005.txt",
              "sha256": "2120d74818efa9cd8fdf3d04ffe62b4dd8d0a798516186532489f4f9b6350b7a",
              "size_bytes": 2035
            },
            "image": {
              "path": "pages/page-0005.png",
              "sha256": "1df6483b3f4a68b7ce8a2068126032aabcb5878d52bc026f66e2bade8b486fa7",
              "size_bytes": 242909
            },
            "native_start": 172,
            "native_end": 646,
            "text": "(2)    For elections that must be coordinated pursuant to section 20 (3)(b) of article X of the \nColorado constitution where the enabling legislation does not require that the electors be \nregistered electors, the political subdivision may conduct its elections pursuant to the enabling \nlegislation but it must assure that the notice required by part 9 of article 7 of this title is provided \nto the election official responsible for publishing the ballot issue notice. \n \n",
            "text_sha256": "d468d47082c91329d0b8988bcf203f10aed233a7d57b275d90299c432211fdf7",
            "visible_location": "Paragraph labeled(2)",
            "source_review_qualification": "",
            "byte_basis": "half_open_utf8_offsets_in_unchanged_native_page"
          }
        ],
        "text": "(2)    For elections that must be coordinated pursuant to section 20 (3)(b) of article X of the \nColorado constitution where the enabling legislation does not require that the electors be \nregistered electors, the political subdivision may conduct its elections pursuant to the enabling \nlegislation but it must assure that the notice required by part 9 of article 7 of this title is provided \nto the election official responsible for publishing the ballot issue notice. \n \n",
        "text_sha256": "d468d47082c91329d0b8988bcf203f10aed233a7d57b275d90299c432211fdf7",
        "continuation_note": null,
        "byte_basis": "ordered_native_fragments_concatenated_without_insertions"
      }
    ],
